  "task_problem_statement": "DATE_ADD function with 3 arguments causes UnboundLocalError\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen using the DATE_ADD function with 3 arguments (unit, value, expression) in Spark dialect, an UnboundLocalError is raised due to a variable being referenced before assignment.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport sqlglot\n\n# This should work but raises UnboundLocalError\nsql = \"SELECT DATE_ADD(MONTH, 20, col)\"\nresult = sqlglot.transpile(sql, read=\"spark\", write=\"spark\")\nprint(result)\n```\n\nThe error occurs when parsing DATE_ADD/DATEADD/TIMESTAMPADD functions with the signature `(unit, value integer, expr)` as documented in the Databricks SQL reference.\n\n#### Expected Behavior\n\nThe function should parse correctly and return the expected SQL output without errors.\n\n#### Actual Behavior\n\n```\nUnboundLocalError: cannot access local variable 'expression' where it is not defined\n```\n\nThis happens because the variable `expression` is being used before it's assigned when processing the 3-argument form of DATE_ADD.",
